{"id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#ends","title":"ends","path":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature.md","line":168,"body":"","kind":"proof","status":"not_started","tex":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature.tex#ends","uses":["[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries#def:geodesic]]","[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries#thm:hopf-rinow]]","[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch01_Preliminaries#def:exponential-map]]","[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:minimizing-segment-exists]]","[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#def:has-min-segments]]","[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:ray-exists-metric]]","[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:line-exists-metric]]","[[references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#def:space-of-ends]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature.tex","label":"ends","line":325,"source":"\\label{ends}\n\n\n\n\nIf $M$ is complete, connected, and noncompact, then every $p\\in M$ is\nthe initial point of a minimizing ray. If $M$ has more than one end, it\nalso contains a minimizing line.\n\\end{lemma}\n\\begin{proof}\n\\sketch\n\n\\uses{def:geodesic,thm:hopf-rinow,def:exponential-map,lem:minimizing-segment-exists,def:has-min-segments,lem:ray-exists-metric,lem:line-exists-metric,def:space-of-ends}\nLemma~\\ref{lem:minimizing-segment-exists} gives minimizing segments.\nHopf--Rinow and the exponential map identify each closed ball with the\nimage of the compact tangent ball of the same radius, so $M$ is proper.\nApply Lemma~\\ref{lem:ray-exists-metric}, and, when there are two ends,\nLemma~\\ref{lem:line-exists-metric}.\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-656e6473\"></span> <p></p>If <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$M$\">$M$</span> is complete, connected, and noncompact, then every <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$p\\in M$\">$p\\in M$</span> is the initial point of a minimizing ray. If <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$M$\">$M$</span> has more than one end, it also contains a minimizing line.  <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p>\\sketch </p><p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh01_Preliminaries%23def%3Ageodesic\">↗ def:geodesic</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh01_Preliminaries%23thm%3Ahopf-rinow\">↗ thm:hopf-rinow</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh01_Preliminaries%23def%3Aexponential-map\">↗ def:exponential-map</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature%23lem%3Aminimizing-segment-exists\">↗ lem:minimizing-segment-exists</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature%23def%3Ahas-min-segments\">↗ def:has-min-segments</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature%23lem%3Aray-exists-metric\">↗ lem:ray-exists-metric</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature%23lem%3Aline-exists-metric\">↗ lem:line-exists-metric</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature%23def%3Aspace-of-ends\">↗ def:space-of-ends</a> Lemma <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature%23lem%3Aminimizing-segment-exists\" data-tex-node=\"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:minimizing-segment-exists\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a6d696e696d697a696e672d7365676d656e742d657869737473\">2</a> gives minimizing segments. Hopf–Rinow and the exponential map identify each closed ball with the image of the compact tangent ball of the same radius, so <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$M$\">$M$</span> is proper. Apply Lemma <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature%23lem%3Aray-exists-metric\" data-tex-node=\"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:ray-exists-metric\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a7261792d6578697374732d6d6574726963\">1</a>, and, when there are two ends, Lemma <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FMorganTian%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature%23lem%3Aline-exists-metric\" data-tex-node=\"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:line-exists-metric\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a6c696e652d6578697374732d6d6574726963\">1</a>. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#lem:ends-exist","next":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch02_ManifoldsNonNegativeCurvature#def:busemann-approx","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/MorganTian/blueprint/src/chapters